@startuml Idea_Tags_and_Stage_Data_Model
' Edison UPM - Tag and development stage model of an Idea (Sprint 2, task #106, US #72)
' Documents what is implemented:
'  - backend: model/IdeaTag.java, model/DevelopmentStage.java, model/Idea.java, service/IdeaService.java
'  - database: database/01_schema.sql (idea_tags, idea_stage)
'  - frontend display labels: frontend/src/utils/ideaDisplay.ts (TAG_LABELS, STAGE_LABELS)

title Edison UPM - Idea Tags and Development Stage Data Model (Sprint 2)

skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam dpi 130
skinparam nodesep 80
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #F1F1F1
  BorderColor #555555
  AttributeFontSize 11
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #333333
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #555555
}
hide circle
hide empty methods

' ================= CLASS MODEL (backend) =================
package "Class model (backend)" as CLASSES {

  class Idea {
    id : UUID
    title : String
    status : IdeaStatus
    .. other attributes omitted ..
    tags : Set<IdeaTag> {0..3, 1..3 to publish}
    developmentStage : DevelopmentStage [0..1] {required to publish}
  }

  enum IdeaTag {
    GREEN_TECH = "Green Tech"
    SOFTWARE = "Software"
    HARDWARE = "Hardware"
    HEALTH_TECH = "HealthTech"
    ED_TECH = "EdTech"
    CIRCULAR_ECONOMY = "Circular Economy"
  }

  enum DevelopmentStage {
    CONCEPT = "Idea"
    PROTOTYPE = "Prototype"
    MVP_LIVE = "MVP live"
  }

  Idea "0..*" --> "0..3" IdeaTag : tags
  Idea "0..*" --> "0..1" DevelopmentStage : developmentStage
}

' ================= ER MODEL (MySQL) =================
package "ER model (MySQL)" as TABLES {

  class ideas <<table>> {
    id : CHAR(36) <<PK>>
    title : VARCHAR(120)
    status : VARCHAR(20)
    .. other columns omitted ..
  }

  class idea_tags <<table>> {
    idea_id : CHAR(36) <<PK, FK>>
    tag : VARCHAR(20) <<PK>>
    --
    CHECK tag IN (GREEN_TECH, SOFTWARE, HARDWARE,
      HEALTH_TECH, ED_TECH, CIRCULAR_ECONOMY)
  }

  class idea_stage <<table>> {
    idea_id : CHAR(36) <<PK, FK>>
    stage : VARCHAR(20)
    --
    CHECK stage IN (CONCEPT, PROTOTYPE, MVP_LIVE)
  }

  ideas "1" *-- "0..*" idea_tags : ON DELETE CASCADE
  ideas "1" *-- "0..1" idea_stage : ON DELETE CASCADE
}

' Each class is stored in the table below it
Idea .down.> ideas : <<persisted in>>
IdeaTag .down.> idea_tags : <<persisted in>>
DevelopmentStage .down.> idea_stage : <<persisted in>>

note right of Idea
  <b>Rules (checked by IdeaService)</b>
  A DRAFT may have 0..3 tags and no stage.
  To publish: 1, 2 or 3 tags and a stage.
  Tags and stage are fixed lists:
  users pick them, never create or edit them.
end note

note bottom of IdeaTag
  <b>API</b> (JSON names)
  tags : ["SOFTWARE", ...]
  developmentStage : "PROTOTYPE"
  Values travel as codes; the label
  (CODE = "Label") is only shown by
  the frontend (ideaDisplay.ts).
  An unknown code → 400 Bad Request.
end note

note bottom of idea_tags
  PK (idea_id, tag): the same tag
  cannot be repeated on an idea.
  The 3-tag limit is not a DB constraint.
end note

note bottom of idea_stage
  PK (idea_id): at most one stage
  per idea. No row until it is chosen.
end note
@enduml
